{# ===========================================================================
   Outbound: PersonWithDisability -> SPDCI DO.DR.03 PersonwithDisability.

   Layout follows the standard: the DO.DR.02 Member block (identity, DRPerson
   demographics, family, socio-economic attributes) sits under `personal_details`;
   status, details, support, transport, housing and programme enrolments sit at
   the root beside it.

   IMPORTANT — the TOP-LEVEL keys of this document are the registry's CONSENT
   SCOPES (clamping is a strict allow-list over them). Adding a key creates a
   scope a partner can be granted; renaming one silently revokes access for
   every partner consented to the old name. The sanity e2e consents to
   `personal_details` and asserts nothing outside its consented scopes comes back.

   Code lists: every enum is translated through the DCI_OUT tables in the
   generated block below (source: register_domain/models/dci_crosswalk.py; keep
   in step with ./scripts/generate-dci-crosswalk.py). No keyword guessing.

   Known limitation: the platform renders with a bare Jinja environment and no
   current date, so "Expired" (CD.DR.14) is emitted only when the stored status
   is EXPIRED; the live comparison against certificate_expiry_date happens in the
   get-disability-status endpoint (partner_api/dr_query.py).

   Child registers arrive under the snake_case of their register mnemonic
   (registry-core `_to_snake_case`): disability_detail, human_assistance,
   assistive_technology, medical_care, housing_support, animal_assistance,
   related_person, program_enrolment.
   =========================================================================== #}
